# b_malformed: a query with a syntax error on purpose (B2).
#
# SPARQL 1.1 Protocol §2.1.7: a query that is not a legal sequence of
# characters in the SPARQL grammar gets HTTP 400. A 200 here means errors are
# reported as success, which a client can only catch by parsing every body.
# The error text that comes back is also the most reliable engine signature.
SELECT ?s WHERE { ?s ?p ?o
